<title>FINLAND: Neste rises on Borealis' Q1 profit.</title>
<headline>Neste rises on Borealis' Q1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish oil group Neste rose sharply on Monday after petrochemicals group Borealis, which it owns half of, reported first quarter pretax profit at 326 million markka, up from 62 million in Q1 1996, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1425/1125 GMT, Neste traded at 136.00 markka, up 5.00 markka or 3.82 percent. Trade was a moderate 2.2 million markka.</p>
<p>&quot;Borealis' profit was quite a lot better than expected,&quot; said one broker.</p>
<p>Borealis' other owner is Norwegian Statoil.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
